// Distributed schedule: 4 compute workers row-band partition the
// outer `i` axis of the SpMV triple loop. Host runs load/save.
// TASK-0341.03.02 AC#3 cell for example 17.
//
// Filed cycle 210 (TASK-0341.03 AC#3 fold-out); attempted cycle
// 212. Structural twin of 07-matmul/distributed (TASK-0297, M5
// AC#4 closeout cycle 118) — same outermost-1D-i-loop +
// per-i-tiled-input + whole-array-broadcast-input shape. The
// TASK-0301 per-data axis-mapping filter (cycle 118) is what makes
// that schedule lower bit-identical:
//   - val[i][k]     — i-tiled on tile (filter retains i)
//   - col_idx[i][k] — i-tiled on tile (filter retains i)
//   - x[j]          — NOT indexed by i (filter excludes i → empty
//                     bounds → whole-array broadcast of x)
//   - y[i]          — i-tiled on gather (filter retains i)
//
// Partition shape
// ---------------
// `loop i : partition=workers;` on the outermost axis. M=8,
// 4 workers, exact-divisible into 2-row bands (0..2, 2..4, 4..6,
// 6..8). Each worker computes y[i_band] using val[i_band][full
// k], col_idx[i_band][full k], and x[full j].
//
// Why this is bit-identical with naive
// ------------------------------------
// The (k, j) inner-fold semantics are unchanged under the i
// partition: each y[i] is the SAME masked-accumulator sum over
// (k, j) regardless of which worker computes it. Workers are
// independent on i; no halo (the data-dependent index lives in
// the kernel body, not in an iv-affine index — there are no
// `i+1` or `i-1` reads anywhere). No cross-worker carry, no
// reduction across i. The existing reference.bin oracle applies
// — no new reference is needed.
//
// Why sync transfers
// ------------------
// Sync-only schedule lowers on every tier-1 backend that supports
// `sync` (pthreads-sync, mp-tcp-bufsync, mp-tcp-poll, openmp-rs).
// Async variants (pthreads-async, mp-tcp-event, mp-uds-event) can
// host this same schedule by capability-match on sync; same shape
// as 07-matmul/distributed.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_val     on host;
    place load_col_idx on host;
    place load_x       on host;
    place save_y       on host;
    place spmv_step    on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Row-band partition the outer i axis. M=8, 4 workers ⇒ 2 rows
    // each, exact-divisible (no TASK-0262 floor-with-spillover
    // remainder).
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // All sync transfers. val + col_idx are i-banded by the
    // axis-mapping filter (i appears in their leading index); x
    // is whole-array broadcast (i absent from x's index → empty
    // tile bounds → broadcast); y is i-banded on gather.
    transfer val     : sync;
    transfer col_idx : sync;
    transfer x       : sync;
    transfer y       : sync;
}
